  :adr/body "# ADR-2607231900: Russian-fleet vessel view — 3-axis OR filter over the existing etzhayyim maritime cluster, no new repo\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-23\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (agent-executed, standing authorization)\n**Related**: ADR-2607203000 (system-dynamics uncomputable-until-measured principle),\n`com-etzhayyim-app-vessel` (IMO vessel registry, ~105K merchant vessels),\n`com-etzhayyim-app-sanctions` (sanctions registry, entityType \"vessel\" + IMO\nidentifiers), `com-etzhayyim-oil-shipping` (tanker commercial wrapper,\ndark-fleet — manifest-only as of 2026-07-23), etzhayyim ADR-0013\n(vessel ↔ oil-shipping cross-actor, dual-DID dark-fleet design).\n\n## Context\n\nThe repository owner asked whether a repo exists that registers/records all\nRussian vessels among the world's fleet. Investigation found that NO single\ndedicated \"Russian vessel registry\" repo exists, but the existing etzhayyim\nmaritime cluster already holds the necessary registries:\n\n- `com-etzhayyim-app-vessel` — `vessel.etzhayyim.com`, physical vessel asset\n  registry keyed by IMO 7-digit number (path-based DID). Covers ~105K merchant\n  vessels (IMO + Lloyd's). AT-Protocol collections include\n  `com.etzhayyim.apps.vessel.ship` and `...shipRegistry` (carries flag). AIS\n  position, voyage, port-call, and owner linkage via cross-actor design.\n- `com-etzhayyim-app-sanctions` — sanctions-list reference registry.\n  `SanctionEntryRecord` has\n  `entityType ∈ {individual, entity, vessel, aircraft, other}` and\n  `identifiers: string[]` described as \"passport / IMO / tax-id as printed on\n  the list\". List sources: OFAC-SDN, OFAC-CONS, EU, UN, JP-MOF, UK-OFSI,\n  CA-OSFI, AU-DFAT. So sanctioned vessels are already recordable by IMO.\n- `com-etzhayyim-oil-shipping` — `oil-shipping.tanker`, the commercial wrapper\n  (charter/operator/**dark-fleet flag**) per etzhayyim ADR-0013's dual-DID design\n  (physical `did:web:vessel.etzhayyim.com:imo:{IMO}` vs commercial\n  `did:web:oil-shipping.etzhayyim.com:tanker:imo:{IMO}`). **As of 2026-07-23 this\n  repo is manifest-only** (`.well-known`, `actor-manifest.jsonld`, tests only) —\n  the tanker schema carrying the dark-fleet flag is NOT yet implemented.\n\nThe three use-cases the owner named (sanctions screening / logistics tracking /\nshadow-fleet monitoring) are all expressible as different views over this same\ncluster. The question became: how to materialize a \"Russian vessel\" view WITHOUT\nbuilding a duplicate registry.\n\n## Decision\n\nImplement the Russian-vessel view as a **query-time OR filter over the existing\ncluster — no new repo, no new entity, no new app**. A vessel is \"Russian\" iff it\nmatches ANY of three axes, joined by IMO 7-digit number:\n\n1. **flag=RUS** — `shipRegistry.flag == \"RU\"` (ISO 3166-1 alpha-2) in\n   `com-etzhayyim-app-vessel`.\n2. **dark-fleet** — the tanker's dark-fleet flag in `com-etzhayyim-oil-shipping`\n   (per etzhayyim ADR-0013). Catches flag-of-convenience shadow tankers that a\n   pure flag filter misses.\n3. **sanctions vessel** — a `SanctionEntryRecord` with `entityType == \"vessel\"`\n   and a 7-digit IMO in `identifiers[]` in `com-etzhayyim-app-sanctions`.\n\n`russian-fleet = flag-axis ∪ dark-fleet-axis ∪ sanctions-axis` (set union over\nIMO). The owner explicitly chose the widest 3-axis definition AND the minimal\n\"query-time filter only\" implementation form.\n\nThe join lives as a pure function at the call site that already aggregates the\nthree registries (the sanctions screening function, which stays the etzhayyim\nregulated function per app-sanctions' own custody/liability split note). No cache\ntable, no materialized index, no new AT-Protocol collection.\n\n## Verification\n\nA pure-logic proving slice (`/tmp/russian_fleet_proof.cljs`, run with nbb, no real\ndata connection) was executed on 2026-07-23 to prove the 3-axis OR resolves\ncorrectly by IMO. The fixture mirrors the three registries' real record shapes\n(numeric IMO on vessels/tankers; `string[]` identifiers on sanctions entries,\nnormalized to numeric IMO at the join):\n\n```clojure\n(defn flag-axis-imos [vessels]\n  (->> vessels (filter #(= \"RU\" (:flag %))) (map :imo) (filter imo?) set))\n\n(defn dark-fleet-axis-imos [tankers]\n  (->> tankers (filter :dark-fleet?) (map :imo) (filter imo?) set))\n\n(defn sanctions-axis-imos [entries]\n  (->> entries (filter #(= \"vessel\" (:entity-type %)))\n       (mapcat :identifiers) (filter imo?) (map #(js/parseInt % 10)) set))\n\n(defn russian-fleet-imos [vessels tankers entries]\n  (set/union (flag-axis-imos vessels)\n             (dark-fleet-axis-imos tankers)\n             (sanctions-axis-imos entries)))\n```\n\nResult (nbb, exit 0):\n\n```\nflag-axis       : #{1111111}\ndark-fleet-axis : #{2222222}\nsanctions-axis  : #{3333333}\nrussian-fleet   : (1111111 2222222 3333333)\nPASS: 3-axis OR resolves (flag=RU ∪ dark-fleet ∪ sanctions-vessel) by IMO.\n```\n\nThe fixture deliberately includes a PA-flag shadow tanker (IMO 2222222) and an\nLR-flag sanctioned vessel (IMO 3333333) — **both MISSED by a flag=RUS-only\nfilter, both CAUGHT by the dark-fleet and sanctions axes respectively**. This is\nthe concrete value of the 3-axis OR over a single-axis flag filter.\n\n## Consequences\n\n(+) Zero new repos, entities, apps, or AT-Protocol collections. The view is a\nfunction over three existing registries.\n\n(+) Catches flag-of-convenience shadow fleet (axis 2) and sanctioned-but-\nreflagged vessels (axis 3) that a flag=RUS-only filter structurally misses —\nproven on the fixture above.\n\n(-) Axis 2 (dark-fleet) is **:uncomputable-until-measured** (ADR-2607203000):\n`com-etzhayyim-oil-shipping` is manifest-only as of 2026-07-23, so the tanker\ndark-fleet flag has no real data yet. The 3-axis OR is structurally complete but\nthe dark-fleet axis yields no real IMOs until oil-shipping lands its tanker\nschema. This is stated, not hidden.\n\n(-) Query-time filter means each query scans the three registries and unions. At\n~105K vessels this is acceptable for on-demand queries; if continuous monitoring\nbecomes a hard requirement, a materialized RussianFleetIndex (rejected here as\noverkill) can be revisited as a follow-up — NOT silently introduced.\n\n(-) The join is only as current as the three underlying registries. Real AIS\nposition ingest (`kotodama ingest/vessel.py`) and real sanctions-list refresh\ncadence are separate concerns outside this ADR's \"view\" scope.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n| Option | Verdict | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| Open a new dedicated \"Russian vessel registry\" repo | ❌ | Duplicates data already in the 105K vessel registry + sanctions registry; creates a sync/split-brain problem; the owner's question was answerable with a view, not a store |\n| Materialize a RussianVesselIndex cache entity | ❌ | Overkill for the chosen query-time-filter form; introduces staleness/sync cost the owner did not ask for |\n| flag=RUS only (single axis) | ❌ | Structurally misses the shadow fleet: Russian-controlled tankers reflagged to Panama/Liberia/etc. would be invisible — the exact gap the dark-fleet + sanctions axes exist to close |\n| Wait for oil-shipping before defining the view | ❌ | The 3-axis logic is provable now; declaring axis 2 :uncomputable-until-measured is more honest than pretending the view must wait |\n\n## References\n\n- `com-etzhayyim-app-vessel` CLAUDE.md + `appview/vessel-registry-v3ss3l01/kotodama.jsonld`\n- `com-etzhayyim-app-sanctions/kotoba/src/{registry,types}.ts` (entityType \"vessel\", identifiers incl. IMO)\n- `com-etzhayyim-oil-shipping` (manifest-only; dark-fleet flag not yet implemented)\n- etzhayyim ADR-0013 (vessel ↔ oil-shipping dual-DID cross-actor, dark-fleet design)\n- ADR-2607203000 (uncomputable-until-measured principle)\n"
